WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:06.694
This gate supports two controls in
NIST special publication eight hundred

3
00:00:06.694 --> 00:00:11.533
fifty-three: I A two, enhancement
twelve, acceptance of PIV credentials,

4
00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:15.788
and I A five, enhancement two,
public key-based authentication.

5
00:00:15.788 --> 00:00:20.462
It supports SCuBA's two
phishing-resistant multifactor policies,

6
00:00:20.462 --> 00:00:25.562
three point one and three point
six, which BOD 25-01 requires.

7
00:00:25.562 --> 00:00:30.520
And it supports FIPS two oh one dash
three's issuance and termination rules,

8
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.599
and special publication eight
hundred sixty-three dash four.

9
00:00:34.599 --> 00:00:38.775
Your organization still sets the
organization-defined parameters,

10
00:00:38.775 --> 00:00:41.925
and the assessor decides
whether each is satisfied.

11
00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:46.860
The evidence an ISSO keeps for Gate
5: the configuration export and

12
00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.975
the check's findings and manifest,
dated, with each list's measurement.

13
00:00:51.975 --> 00:00:56.475
The C B nine and C B ten rows,
beside the ScubaGear report.

14
00:00:56.475 --> 00:01:01.863
Lab 2's refused sign-in, with the revocation
record and the list that published it.

15
00:01:01.863 --> 00:01:03.960
And the mode rules in the export.
